  "result": "Perfect! I found the source file that decides what number a newly created issue is given.\n\nLooking at the code flow:\n1. When creating an issue, `createIssue` in `issue-service.ts` calls `issueRepo.nextIssueNumber()`\n2. This function is defined in `issue-repository.ts` and queries the database to find the maximum issue number for that specific project\n3. It returns `max + 1`, ensuring per-project numbering starting at 1\n\nThe `nextIssueNumber` function (lines 292-304) implements the logic: it queries for the maximum issue number within the specific project and organization, then increments it. When no issues exist in a project yet, max returns null (treated as 0), so the first issue gets number 1. This ensures each project maintains its own independent sequence, which is why PLAT-42 and another project can both have their own sequences.\n\nANSWER: src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts",
